<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  fuaran-live consumes the `Fuaran.Core.*` spine packages from the shared
  workspace local feed for inner-loop iteration, alongside nuget.org for the
  Fable stack. The relative
  `../../../local-nuget-feed` path assumes this repo lives under the shared
  workspace root as a sibling of the other Fuaran-UI repos —
  the same convention the `fuaran` tier's nuget.config uses. Forward slash for
  Linux CI portability (a backslash is a literal filename character there).

  SOURCE ORDER IS DELIBERATE: `nuget.org` is declared FIRST and `local` second,
  which is the reverse of the sibling repos. NuGet prefers the earlier-declared
  source for the same id+version, so this repo resolves the RELEASED copy of a
  package whenever one exists at the pinned version.

  That is the right order for this repo specifically, and for one reason: this
  playground's whole posture is that it restores anonymously, exactly as a
  public consumer would. A released-first order means a maintainer's build
  resolves what a stranger's build resolves. Under the sibling order it would
  not: a package the maintainer happened to have packed locally would shadow
  the released one, and the first person to notice the difference would be
  someone who cannot reproduce it.

  What it costs locally, stated plainly so nobody rediscovers it as a bug: a
  fresh local pack does NOT shadow a same-version released package here. To
  iterate against unreleased local changes, advance the package version (the
  released feed has no such version, so `local` is the only source that can
  serve it) — or flip these two lines temporarily and flip them back. Do not
  flip them permanently: the anonymous-restore fidelity above is the property
  being protected, and it is only ever worth what it is trusted to be.

  In CI this order changes nothing either way — the workflow mints an empty
  local feed, so nuget.org is the only source that can serve anything.
-->
<configuration>
  <packageSources>
    <add key="nuget.org" value="https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json" />
    <add key="local" value="../../../local-nuget-feed" />
  </packageSources>
</configuration>
